'''''BeamNG.drive''''' is a [[vehicle simulation game|sandbox vehicle simulation video game]] developed and published by [[Bremen]]-based [[video game developer]] BeamNG GmbH for [[Windows]], [[Linux]], and [[PlayStation 5]]. The game features [[Soft-body dynamics|soft-body physics]] to simulate realistic handling and damage to [[vehicle]]s.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.beamng.com/game/|title=BeamNG.drive – BeamNG|language=en-US|access-date=2026-09-26|archive-date=2026-09-24|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260924175446/https://www.beamng.com/game/|url-status=live|website=BeamNG |date=29 July 2026 }}</ref><ref name="bng-ign"/><ref name="BBC"/> Initially released as a [[tech demo]] on August 3, 2013, along with paid access to an [[Alpha (software)|alpha]], it was later made available on [[Steam Early Access]] for Windows on May 29, 2015. The game was released for the [[PlayStation 5]] on October 19, 2026.<ref name="PlayStation">{{cite web|url=https://blog.playstation.com/2026/05/28/beamng-drive-speeds-onto-ps5-this-year/ |title=BeamNG.drive speeds onto PS5 this year |date=28 May 2026 |access-date=28 May 2026 |first=Thomas |last=Fischer |website=Playstation.Blog}}</ref><ref name=ps5>{{Cite web |title=PS5™ Release Date Announcement |date=24 September 2026 |url=https://beamng.com/game/news/announce/ps5-release-date |website=BeamNG.com}}</ref> BeamNG also develops a [[project fork|fork]] of the game [[serious game|designed for education as well as industrial and academic research]] entitled '''''BeamNG.tech'''''.<ref name="BNG-tech1">{{Cite tech report|last1=Maul|first1=Pascale|last2=Mueller|first2=Marc|last3=Enkler|first3=Fabian|last4=Pigova|first4=Eva|last5=Fischer|first5=Thomas|last6=Stamatogiannakis|first6=Lefteris|place=Bremen, Germany|website=BeamNG.tech|title=BeamNG.tech Technical Paper|date=2021-06-21|publisher=BeamNG GmbH|url=https://beamng.tech/blog/2021-06-21-beamng-tech-whitepaper/bng_technical_paper.pdf|access-date=2024-01-17|language=en}}</ref>
